am of 798, and although 1932 becomes reachable at t=33775 (only via 5000\u201312000-unit gaps, already violating the delta), its single contact with 131 precedes that arrival. The negative result stems from event ordering, not from low volume or missing structure."}, "raw_final_response": "**Findings**\n\n- Static connectivity exists: 798\u2192389 (step_14) and 389 is a hub with 151 partners (step_08), and 131 is 2 hops from 798 ignoring time (step_07). So a time-ignoring path exists \u2014 but that is not enough.\n- With the 600-unit relay constraint, only 3 nodes are reachable from 798 and 131 is not among them (step_01).\n- Even with **no** waiting limit, 798 temporally reaches 650 nodes but not 131 (step_03), and no time-respecting route exists (step_13).\n- Mechanistic reason: 131's only *incoming* contacts come from 972, 1877, 1932 (step_06). 972 and 1877 are never temporally reachable from 798 (step_09, step_11). 1932 *is* reachable, but only at t=33775 via huge waits of 5432/5024/11927 units (step_10), and after 33775 no time-respecting path 1932\u2192131 exists (step_17) \u2014 1932's contact with 131 (single event, step_12) happened earlier. Also 389 cannot reach 131 after 798's contact at t=11392 (step_18).\n- Confounders controlled: ample overall activity (4954 events, 1888 nodes; step_02), hub popularity of 389 (step_08), and 131 was active throughout the middle of the window (step_19) \u2014 so the failure is not from sparsity or inactivity, but from event ordering.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_d7716db7\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [798, 131, 389, 1932, 972, 1877],\n  \"window\": [4302, 42701],\n  \"confidence\": 0.92,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_17\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_18\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_19\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"A static 798\u2192389\u2192131 connection exists and both endpoints are active, but no time-respecting sequence carries influence from 798 to 131 \u2014 not even with unlimited waiting, let alone the 600-unit relay limit. 131 only ever receives from 972, 1877 and 1932; the first two are never temporally downstream of 798, and although 1932 becomes reachable at t=33775 (only via 5000\u201312000-unit gaps, already violating the delta), its single contact with 131 precedes that arrival. The negative result stems from event ordering, not from low volume or missing structure.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 58607, "total_output_tokens": 4447, "total_tokens": 63054, "total_latency_ms": 69216, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}